Description:
**Professional Internship: Hardware Development (M/F/Div.)**


* Full-time
* Legal Entity: Home Comfort


**Company Description**

The Bosch Group has more than 400 000 employees around the world, present in 60 countries, and we are proud to impact people’s lives and to work towards a more sustainable future.   
In the city of Aveiro, Bosch has one of its biggest production sites for Bosch Home Comfort division, as well as a Research and Development Center for new and improved heating solutions for the residential segment. With more than 1400 employees, focused on innovation, sustainability and collaboration, Bosch Aveiro joins together experts in diverse areas, from mechanical engineering to connectivity and software solutions, as well as industrialization and quality.   
At Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our promise to our associates is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and we inspire each other. Join in and feel the difference in mindsets, cultures, generations, identities and perspectives. Everyone should bring their authenticity and work together respectfully. By including everyone and ensuring equal opportunities we unleash our full potential. 


**Job Description**

**Your contribution to something big:**

This position offers the opportunity to be part of the department HC-CS/XCT (Home Comfort / Combustion Systems / Engineering Controls) which is responsible for the development of control units for heating appliances. Within the department several SAFe trains have been set up consisting of multidisciplinary scrum teams, responsible for Hardware (mechanical and electrical) and Software (control application and embedded) development.

As Hardware Engineer you are involved in the entire hardware development process, from drawing up requirements up to maintenance of the product in series production. 


**Your responsibilities**

* Design, develop and test electronics;
* Documenting solutions directions and design, specifically with safety related parts;
* Recognize possible process and product improvements and actively implement such improvements;
* Selection of components, drawing schematics (including simulations) and re-viewing of PCB lay-outs;
* Verification and integration testing;
* Provide support and problem solving during EMC testing;
* Active participation and contributing to all design related activities. 


**Qualifications**

**What distinguishes you:** 

* Education: Academic degree in Electrical/Electronic Engineering; 
* Personality: Result-oriented, creative and strong in communication;
* Enjoy working in an internationally distributed development team (e.g. PT, NL, DE, IN) and want to make a difference;
* Working method: Highly self-motivated, flexible, with focus on continuous improvement and learning, and ability to understand complex systems;
* Enthusiasm: have passion and interest in the latest trends and technologies in the electronics industry;
* Languages: good Portuguese and English knowledge, both written and spoken.


**Additional Information**

**Work #LikeABosch includes:**   

Challenges in an international environment | Flexible work conditions | Exchange with colleagues around the world | Medical office on site (general surgeon, psychology, physiotherapy, general clinic) | Sports and health related activities | Free parking lot | Canteen


**Success stories don´t just happen. They are made...**

**Make it happen! We are looking forward to your application!**


