**DevOps Developer with Python for ADAS Computing Platform**


* Full-time
* Legal Entity: Robert Bosch S.R.L.


**Company Description**

For over 30 years, at Bosch Romania we nurture, build and sustain enduring relationships, to enable direct operational strategic benefits to our customers across the country. Our headquarters located in Bucharest develops and supports the company’s **medium and long-term sales strategy**, thus promoting sustainable growth in areas such as Mobility, Consumer Goods and Energy and Building Technology. Through various professional and personal development opportunities, flexible working conditions, modern offices in Bucharest and Sibiu, we are one of the most desired employers among professionals in Romania. Our promise to our colleagues is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and inspire each other. Join us and see the difference. **Work # LikeABosch**


**Job Description**

We are currently looking for a DevOps Engineer to join our Continuous Integration/Continuous Development (CI/CD) team.

In the Hardware related Software Group, we are building the next generation of ADAS Computing Platform to be used for Driver Assistance Systems and Automated Driving.

We are responsible for Prototype microprocessor and microcontroller software development, bring-up and BSP development of state-of-the-art SoC (Systems on a Chip). We are also integrating the software solutions in customer projects and bringing them to series production.


**In your role you will:**

* Develop CI/CD solutions as platform solution;
* Develop the DevOps solution based on Azure DevOps and GitHub;
* Integrate and configure the CI/CD platform solutions in the Customer Projects;
* Develop and implement Build infrastructure (CONAN, CMAKE);
* Discuss and align with internal Micro-controller, Micro-processor and InterSOC teams;
* Contribute to definition of generic concepts of automation;
* Communicate with development partners and customers.


**Technology Stack:**

* Jenkins, Azure DevOps;
* Python, Bash, Powershell;
* GitHub;
* Linux;
* Docker;
* AGILE Methodology.


**Qualifications**

* You have a Bachelor or master’s degree in computer science, Automation Electronics and Telecommunications, Informatics, Mathematics or comparable;
* You have **2+ years of experience** in Continuous Integration, Continuous development;
* Previous experience setting up or maintaining **CI pipelines (Jenkins, Azure DevOps,** etc**.**);
* Good **Scripting knowledge** (Bash, Python, PowerShell);
* Basic **Linux** knowledge;
* Basic **Embedded C** knowledge;
* You have a **Proactive mentality** and high level of **flexibility** for AGILE working;
* You have an **Open communication** and **Open Feedback** mindset;
* You are eager to **learn** and develop yourself;
* English – a good level is mandatory.


**Nice to have:**

* Build infrastructure experience (CONAN, CMAKE);
* Good **C++** and **Embedded C** knowledge.


**Additional Information**

***#LikeABosch Benefits:***

Your work-life balance is valuable to us, so we offer you:

* **25 Days of annual leave**, because work-life balance is essential to us; 
* **Flexible working hours**, but if you want to work from somewhere else, feel free, our **Home Office** program helps you do that.

Your **health** and **well-being** is important to us, so we have you covered:

* Medical subscription;
* Accident insurance;
* Sport activities and well-being initiatives.

We believe in a **Life-Long Learning** approach, so you can take advantage of:

* Technical and soft skills trainings;
* Access to e-learning platforms;
* Local and Global career development programs;
* Opportunity to attend conferences;
* Bookster subscription.

You will be part of a **product company**. You will contribute to developing end-to-end products that are delivered to Global OEMs.


**On top of these, we are offering:**

* A monthly budget which can be used for several different services on an online benefit platform;
* Annual bonus;
* Lunch discounts.

Ready to work **#LikeABosch**

We live by our values, have an open feedback culture and there is plenty of room for innovative ideas. All because a team is only as valuable as its members.


