**Company Description**

The Bosch Group has more than 400 000 employees around the world, present in 60 countries, and we are proud to impact people’s lives and to work towards a more sustainable future.   
In the city of Aveiro, Bosch has one of its biggest production sites for Bosch Home Comfort division, as well as a Research and Development Center for new and improved heating solutions for the residential segment. With more than 1400 employees, focused on innovation, sustainability and collaboration, Bosch Aveiro joins together experts in diverse areas, from mechanical engineering to connectivity and software solutions, as well as industrialization and quality.   
At Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our promise to our associates is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and we inspire each other. Join in and feel the difference in mindsets, cultures, generations, identities and perspectives. Everyone should bring their authenticity and work together respectfully. By including everyone and ensuring equal opportunities we unleash our full potential. 


**Job Description**

**Your contribution to something big:**

We are an international and multi-cultural team spread over several locations e.g. in China, Germany, India, Portugal and the Netherlands. As part of Software Excellence Team in the SW EPQ team you will ensure software quality for next generation of IoT HVAC products for complete life cycle at Home Comfort Group.

Our services enable our customers (Software development teams) to focus on their actual work.


**Your Responsibilities**

* Ensure software quality for next generation of IoT HVAC products for complete life cycle;
* Responsible person for Software Product Quality and ensure that the Software development framework is instantiated accordingly to the need of team's specific SW products;
+ All primary SW development domains used for those kind of SW products (e.g. embedded, frontend, backend, mobile applications);
* Support in development of software quality strategies in software development;
* Preparation and execution of SW trainings;
* Cooperation responsible consultancy in improvement of SW development processes in engineering;
* Planning and execution of SW assessments, such as:
+ QG (Quality gates)
+ Quality of used methods
+ Quality of development processes
* Cooperation with other central Bosch SW organizations;
* Field observation and processing of data;
* SW-Quality reporting to management.


**Qualifications**

**What distinguishes you:** 

* **Education:** Degree in the field of software engineering, computer science or equivalent;
* **Experience:** Experience in software quality management, both with embedded SW and non-embedded software (e.g. Mobile Applications, Frontend, Backend);
* Own experience in verification and validation (test and review);
* Handling the area of tension between SW-QM (verification & validation) and project management (e.g. Classical, Agile);
* Practical experience in the development of SW products in different programming languages (e.g. C, C#, Java, scripting languages) and modeling languages (e.g. Matlab);
* Experience in monitoring and tracking of SW quality topics (e.g. defect flow model, technical debt);
* Experience in the implementation of maturity models (e.g. CMMI, Spice);
* Experience of software quality management in international environments (is an advantage);
* **Know how:** Knowledge of Atlassian tools JIRA including Jira System Administration, Jira SDK, API;
* Knowledge of data communication in wired and wireless embedded software solutions is a plus (e.g. RF, Zigbee, BLE, WiFi);
* Familiarity with integrated software development environments (e.g. IDE, CI & AB, FOSS communities);
* SW development responsibility (e.g. experienced SW engineer, project manager, SW architect);
* **Languages:** Fluently English (local language is an advantage);
* **Working Style and Methods:** Continuous training in software engineering and quality topics. Willingness to travel;
* **Personality:** Assertiveness.


