* Full-time
* Legal Entity: Home Comfort


**Company Description**

The Bosch Group has more than 400 000 employees around the world, present in 60 countries, and we are proud to impact people’s lives and to work towards a more sustainable future.

In the city of Aveiro, Bosch has a Research and Development Center with projects for different business areas of the Bosch Group. The Mobility Aftermarket division (MA), that provides the aftermarket and repair shops worldwide with modern diagnostic and repair shop technology, is one of those business areas. Within an Agile set-up of Software Developers, Software Testers, Product Owners, Scrum Masters and UX/UI Designers, the MA division is creating tailor-made solutions to address the service needs of new-generation, electronically controlled and connected vehicle solutions.

At Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our promise to our associates is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and we inspire each other. Join in and feel the difference in mindsets, cultures, generations, identities and perspectives. Everyone should bring their authenticity and work together respectfully. By including everyone and ensuring equal opportunities we unleash our full potential.


**Job Description**

**Your contribution to something big:**

* **Shape the future:** You are designing and implementing modern software designs in an international environment;
* **Create new things:** You are contributing to the successful lifecycle for a variety of Software Applications with specialization in Back-End development;
* **Creativity and leeway:** You are responsible of shaping the software architecture for a variety of products and ensuring the software quality and security according to development guidelines and processes;
* **Take responsibility:** Work in an independent and agile self-organized scrum team in a fast-paced delivery environment;
* **Holistic thinking**: Demonstrated ability for holistic thinking and problem-solving, considering the broader implications of mobile development within the automotive services landscape;
* **Working style**: Structured and solution oriented working style;
* **Personality**: You are a self-starter with a knack for working on Automotive and Mobile technologies and an inclination grow and share your knowledge base of the latest technologies, industry standardization, and engineering best practices.  


As a **Mobile Engineer** you will:

* Collaborate with our development team to design, develop, and maintain mobile applications for Android platforms;  

* Assist in the implementation of new features and enhancements to existing applications;  

* Participate in the full software development lifecycle, including requirements gathering, design, coding, testing, and deployment;  

* Troubleshoot and debug issues to ensure the performance, quality, and responsiveness of our applications;  

* Stay up to date with the latest trends, tools, and technologies in mobile development to continuously improve our products;  

* Embrace cross-platform development principles and explore opportunities to leverage frameworks such as MAUI and Xamarin.


**Qualifications**

**What distinguishes you:** 

* **Education:** Bachelor’s degree in computer science, Engineering, or related field;  

* **Experience:** Some experience with mobile development in Android using Java or Kotlin;  
Cross-platform development experience, especially with Xamarin, is a plus;  
2+ years of experience with C# and .NET programming language is a plus;  

* **Know-how:** Familiarity with software development methodologies and best practices;  

* **Languages:** Proficiency in English;  

* **Working Style and Methods**: A willingness to learn and adapt to new technologies and frameworks;  

* **Personality:** Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail;  
Excellent communication and collaboration abilities.


**Additional Information**

**Work #LikeABosch includes:** 

Flexible work conditions | Hybrid work system | Exchange with colleagues around the world | Health insurance and medical office on site (general surgeon, psychology, physiotherapy, general clinic) | Training opportunities (p.e., technical training, foreign languages training) & certifications | Access to great discounts in partnerships and Bosch products | Sports and health related activities | Free parking lot |Canteen


