** Senior Network Engineer WAN**

Country/Region:   PL               Location:     Cz_stochowa, WP, PL, 42-200   


Req ID 72143 | Cz_stochowa, Poland, ZF Automotive Systems Poland Sp. z o.o.


**About the Team:**

The ZF WAN Team is global network infrastructure team that is taking care of the connectivity of all of ZFs 350+ sites. Currently the WAN is being changed from a Hybrid setup, relying on MPLS and Internet towards an Internet only underlay with SD-WAN. Automation is key in adding value to the company and repetitive tasks are to be replaced.


**What you can look forward:**

* Analysis, design, implementation, and operation of the Wide Area Network (WAN);
* Participation in the definition of standards and processes for the WAN & Participation in future development of the network, e.g. software defined network;
* Consult with application development teams regarding performance of applications in the WAN & Management of external service provider and monitoring of service level agreements;
* Reporting, analysis of infrastructure and requirements, and recommendation of proactive network changes;
* Analysis, processing and tracking of disturbance and performance & problems. Implementation and support of WAN optimization and encryption technology;
* Planning and implementation of version and system changes & Participation in international projects;
* Ability/willingness to meet flexible schedule arrangements per customer requirements (i.e. on-call duty).


**Your Profile:**

* At least bachelor degree in Computer Science or similar field;    
* High sense of responsibility and ownership for the availability and performance of the network infrastructure;   
* Proven analytical abilities in addition to strong troubleshooting and diagnostic skills;   
* Working & knowledge of the OSI network model, Ethernet, and TCP/IP networking;   
* Knowledge and experience working with automation and API tools and languages (Ansible, YAML, Python, JSON, etc…) XML, webservices;   
* Knowledge and experience in network technologies, in particular wide area networkingl   
* Experience with routing protocols (BGP, OSPF);   
* Experience providing customer support and resolution regarding technical issues;   
* Experience in dealing with customers and suppliers.  

* Stable company background and long-term working possibility; 
* International working environment; 
* Professional growth and career opportunities; 
* Private medical care, MyBenefit platform, discounts package on goods and services; 
* Flexible working hours;  
* Possibility of hybrid or remote work (to be agreed); 
* Exposure to modern technologies


