**Company Description**

Let’s turn visions into reality. At Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our areas of activity are every bit as diverse as our outstanding Bosch teams around the world. Their creativity is the key to innovation through connected living, mobility or industry. Our promise to our associates is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and we inspire each other. Join in and feel the difference.  
Every year, several thousands of young people on practical placements with Bosch experience daily work at first hand. With this long term internship opportunity they are actively integrated into projects and are fully incorporated in the daily work of one of the world's largest industrial corporations. The new specialist experience you gather will help you choose the future focus of your studies and the way you wish to launch your professional career. One thing is sure: Exciting and interesting tasks await you!


**Job Description**

*  Responsible for running the processes within the described parameters and the continuous improvement of the process parameters;
*  Responsible for the correct application of the legal norms in force, the Bosch norms as well as the criteria regarding safety and work protection when he intervenes and/or defines the processes;
*  Defines and describes the processes: creates the parameter sheet, based on analyses, tests and/or based on experience from the lead plant and/or specifications received from the supplier;
* Carry out tests, apply the acquired knowledge-lessons learned, document and keep a history of these tests;
* Defines the list of spare parts and the standard of technical maintenance for the improvement brought to the machine;
* Responsible for the preparation of necessary documentation/obtaining process assimilation;
* Draws up process standards in the production lines;
* Has permanent contact with the international production network;
* Defines and monitors the process/production parameters as well as the technical cycle of the process;
* Analyze process deviations and minimize their impact;
* Calculate TEK (technical capacity) according to the rules in force;
* Implements the leadplant standard with reference to the processes in its own area of __activity;
* Defines and improves based on the requirements from the production department, taking into account the legal and Bosch norms in force and QDC (Quality Delivery and Cost);
* Defines and improves based on the analysis from the analysis team or audits from the client;
* Maintains permanent contact with suppliers for possible process improvements;
* Propose improvements for processes/production lines in accordance with the implementation policies or directly from the hierarchical superior.


**Qualifications**

* Technical university degree;
* Experience in Manufacturing;
* Very good English language skills (spoken/written);
* Good knowledge in problem solving;
* Good analytics skills;
* Good communication/ cooperation skills.


