* Optimization of the energy consumption in the machine hardware and software concept. (no lost energy in the machine movements, ventilators are only used when needed, machine deactivates after a few minutes - standby mode);      
* Functional responsibility for: Human Machine Interface Design & Programming; Control valve functionality management & implementation; vision systems & servo controls; PLC hardware; PLC programming; Sensors definition & setup; pneumatic & hydraulic valve actuators control system; design electrical wiring diagrams, hardware controls architecture; processors, I/O, power distribution, motor controls & sensors; cabinet field wiring; mistake proofing design & implementation; configure manufacturing/traceability application(s) for lines/cells;      
* Integration of AI solutions into IRS manufacturing processes. Use cases identification and implementation according to DivR strategy and methodology;      


**Required skills and experience / main competencies**

* Bachelor’s degree from a four-year college or university with academic study/major in Electrical/Electronic/Controls Engineering, Engineering Technology, Technical Science or related field. Minimum 3 years’ experience in the field of design, construction, maintenance or operation in the field of automatic control systems, programming industrial robots, communication network and Ethernet of production processes;      
* Fluency in Portuguese and English language;      
* Proficient in MS-Office package;      
* Knowledge of MES (Manufacturing Execution System), ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning), CMMS (Computerized Maintenance Management Systems), Digital twins (digital copy of a real process) to optimize system design, production and maintenance      
* Familiarity with APQP tools and documentation;      
* Self motivated individual with the ability to work independently. Excellent verbal and written communication skills;      
* Ability to prioritize tasks in line with department goals;      
* Strong project management skills;      
* Design and interpretation of electrical circuits;      
* Knowledge of industry and HS& E regulations;      
* Knowledge of communications protocols;      
* Ability to conduct effective on the job as well as virtual trainings;      
* Availability and readiness for regional and international business trips.      

* You will work in a varied, innovative work environment, in an International team;      
*  Full of challenges and high-level professional activities;      
* Competitive compensation and benefits;      
* Continuous learning opportunities;      
* Discounts for employees with several partners;      
* Flexible working hours.      


