**Company Description**

The Bosch Group has more than 400 000 employees around the world, present in 60 countries, and we are proud to impact people’s lives and to work towards a more sustainable future.   
In the city of Aveiro, Bosch has one of its biggest production sites for Bosch Home Comfort division, as well as a Research and Development Center for new and improved heating solutions for the residential segment. With more than 1400 employees, focused on innovation, sustainability and collaboration, Bosch Aveiro joins together experts in diverse areas, from mechanical engineering to connectivity and software solutions, as well as industrialization and quality.   
At Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our promise to our associates is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and we inspire each other. Join in and feel the difference in mindsets, cultures, generations, identities and perspectives. Everyone should bring their authenticity and work together respectfully. By including everyone and ensuring equal opportunities we unleash our full potential. 


**Job Description**

The Department of "Engineering, Architecture and Systems" of our Combustion Solutions is providing system solutions and tools for in the Bosch Home Comfort Business unit.  
It enables the business units and business enablers to realize their products and services according to the customer needs. Starting with requirements engineering it provides tools and processes for solution concepts, system simulation and integration, verification, and validation (iVV). An important part of the iVV strategy is the “Virtual testing” which allows to verify the customer requirements for a defined solution option in a virtual environment.


**Your contribution to something big:**

* Leading virtual testing activities for our Combustion Solutions (process, tools, alignment);
* Maintenance and build-up of infrastructure (w/ other business units);
* Support and align on DevOps tasks and processes;
* Coordinate simulation activities inside the Combustion Solutions area;
* Support of projects on specific tasks.


**Qualifications**

**What distinguishes you:** 

* **Education:** Degree in Electronic, Mechanical Engineering, Computer Science, Software engineering or Informatics (or similar);
* **Experience and Knowledge:** 
+ Knowledge and experience with model-based development tools (MATLAB and Simulink);
+ Knowledge and interest to understand HVAC systems;
+ Knowledge of modern DevOps, particularly with the Atlassian toolchain (Bitbucket, Jira (R4J, Xray), Confluence), Jenkins. Git and testing experience is valued;
* **Personality:** 
+ Very good communication skills, and willingness to collaborate with an international team - this includes occasional business travels abroad;
+ Good interpersonal skills and teamwork spirit, with eagerness to learn and share knowledge with others;
+ Strong sense of responsibility;
+ Proactive attitude with strategic mindset;
* **Languages****:** Good level of English and Portuguese language written and spoken.


**Additional Information**

**Work #LikeABosch includes:**   

Flexible work conditions | Hybrid work system | Exchange with colleagues around the world | Health insurance and medical office on site (general surgeon, psychology, physiotherapy, general clinic) | Training opportunities (p.e., technical training, foreign languages training) & certifications | Access to great discounts in partnerships and Bosch products | Sports and health related activities | Free parking lot | Canteen


