In our Bosch Energy and Building Solutions division, we provide solutions in the areas of safety, security and smart buildings. Our teams of experts design, implement and manage both standard and customised solutions, in consultation with our customers. We use high-quality and innovative technologies for fire detection, evacuation, (critical audio) communication, burglary prevention, video surveillance, access control and incident management. Discover more at 


**Job Description**

**__ Your Role as a QHSE Manager**

As our QHSE Manager, you're pivotal in ensuring compliance and safety. In addition to overseeing software development, you coordinate external audits, address departmental concerns on health, safety, and the environment, and safeguard confidentiality by promptly addressing security breaches like unattended confidential documents.


**___ Your Tasks**

* Coordinate quality activities and systems to ensure compliance with quality requirements, including registration, analysis, and reporting, as well as implementing preventive and corrective actions;
* Represent BTHN internally within Bosch and externally as needed, serving as a point of contact for quality-related matters;
* Manage certification processes and maintain systems to uphold quality standards;
* Control waste stream processes within the organization;
* Organize and conduct audits for systems, processes, and products according to schedule, including assessments for suppliers and subcontractors;
* Monitor workplace safety procedures, conduct hazard analysis, and implement measures to maintain a safe working environment;
* Serve as the primary contact for environment-related topics, fulfilling legal obligations as an environmental officer and overseeing CO2 performance ladder compliance;
* Act as the Occupational Health & Safety Coordinator for Robert Bosch B.V., overseeing policy implementation, annual planning, OSH committee activities, and coordinating occupational health and safety services.


**Qualifications**

**__ What You Bring**

* Bachelor's degree in Business Administration
* Qualified to conduct both internal and external audits
* Proficiency in quality certifications such as ISO 9001, ISO 14001
* VCA certification
* Familiarity with ARBO regulations and practices


**__What distinguishes you**

* Exceptional collaboration skills and a team-oriented mindset
* Proactive, self-steering attitude towards challenges
* An agile mindset for adaptive problem-solving
* Proficient stakeholder management skills for impactful collaboration
* Currently residing on The Netherlands (mandatory)
* Business fluency in the English language to seamlessly connect with our diverse international community. Additional proficiency in German is highly preferred
* You have a comprehensive background in normalization/standardization methods and quality requirements.
* You exhibit strong analytical abilities, persuasiveness, and adeptness at maintaining an overview while efficiently planning and organizing tasks
* You possess knowledge of audit processes and demonstrate persuasive communication skills


**Additional Information**

**__ What We Offer** 

* A competitive salary ranging from €4500 to €6000 gross per month;
* 25 vacation days + 13 ADV ;
* Pension plan (Metal and Technology);
* A position with a one-year contract and the possibility of a permanent contract;
* Laptop, iPhone, excellent software access, and support/assistance from Bosch's global IT organization;
* A unique and challenging role within an internationally operating company focused on cutting-edge technologies;
* Excellent working atmosphere;
* Opportunities for remote work;
* Extensive training and development opportunities (both on-the-job and through external courses);
* Discounts on Bosch products at the staff store.


**__** **Application Process**

* Telephone introduction with corporate recruiter Madalena; 
* First interview on-site with your future manager; 
* Second interview; 
* Final interview and meet the team;
* Offer and contract at Bosch! 


