Since its establishment in 2013, Bosch Engineering Center Cluj plays an essential role in the current transformation of the mobility sector. Through its extensive expertise in software, hardware & mechanical engineering, reliability engineering, as well as sales planning, the center contributes to the development of innovative products and services based on artificial intelligence (AI) applied in the fields of **automated driving, electric and connected mobility.** Thanks to the diverse professional and personal development opportunities, flexible working conditions, modern offices and laboratories in Cluj-Napoca, Jucu, Bucharest and Sibiu, we are one of the most desired employers among engineers and IT professionals in Romania.


Our promise to our colleagues is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and inspire each other. Join us and see the difference. **Work # LikeABosch**


**Job Description**

We are currently looking for an **Senior Safety Software Developer with Classic AUTOSAR (Cluj, Sibiu)** to work within our teams. 

In the **Hardware related Software Deparment**, we are building the next generation of **ADAS Integration** **Platform** to be used for Driver Assistance Systems and Automated Driving. 

We are responsible for **Prototype software development**, bring-up and low-level software development of state-of-the-art **SoC (Systems on a Chip)**. We are also integrating the software solutions in customer projects and bringing them to series production. 


**In your role you will:**

* Lead the development and implementation of safety-critical software for ADAS projects in compliance with ASIL-D requirements;
* Design and maintain software architecture and detailed software designs, ensuring integration with the Classic AUTOSAR architecture;
* Be part of safety analyses, including FMEA, FMEDA, FTA, and DFA, to identify and mitigate potential risks;
* Develop and implement safety plans, safety cases, and validation and verification strategies in accordance with ASPICE processes;
* Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure the seamless integration of software components and adherence to project timelines and quality standards;
* Stay abreast of industry trends, emerging technologies, and regulatory changes related to automotive software safety;
* Mentor junior engineers and contribute to the continuous improvement of our safety processes and methodologies;
* Integrate ECU Extract, Configure BSW modules, Configure and Generate RTE;. 
* Integrate application components into the software;
* Deliver the committed work package within the agreed time and quality; 
* Proactively communicate delays or problems occurred during development;
* Conduct reviews (requirements, design, code, module test);
* Follow the defined software development processes, while proactively pushing to improve and streamline all areas of the process. 


**Technology Stack:**

* AUTOSAR;
* Hardware Based Software: Embedded OS, Multicore MCU, System Control;
* Safety Stack, E2E, Ethernet, CAN, CAN-FD, XCP, UDS; 
* Git, Doors, CANoe;
* Knowledge of ASPICE; 
* ISO26262.


**Qualifications**

* Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related field;
* Minimum of 7 years of experience in automotive software development, with a strong focus on safety-critical systems;
* In-depth knowledge of Classic AUTOSAR architecture and its application in automotive projects;
* Proven experience in developing software compliant with ASIL-D safety standards;
* Solid understanding of the ASPICE process and its application in automotive software development;
* Proficiency in safety analysis techniques, including FMEA, FTA, and DFA;
* Strong programming skills in C/C++ and familiarity with software development tools and environments;
* Excellent problem-solving abilities, strong communication skills, and the ability to work effectively in a team-oriented environment;
* Fluent in English, both written and spoken.


