At Bosch, we shape the future by inventing high-quality technologies and services that spark enthusiasm and enrich people’s lives. Our promise to our associates is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and we inspire each other. Join in and feel the difference in mindsets, cultures, generations, identities and perspectives. Everyone should bring their authenticity and work together respectfully. By including everyone and ensuring equal opportunities we unleash our full potential. 


**Job Description**

**Your contribution to something big:**

This position offers the opportunity to be part of the department HC-CS/XCT (Home Comfort / Combustion Systems / Engineering Controls) which is responsible for the development of control units for heating appliances. Within the department several SAFe trains have been set up consisting of multidisciplinary scrum teams, responsible for Hardware (mechanical and electrical) and Software (control application and embedded) development.

As Hardware Engineer you are involved in the entire hardware development process, from drawing up requirements up to maintenance of the product in series production. 


**Your responsibilities**

* Design, develop and test electronics;
* Documenting solutions directions and design, specifically with safety related parts;
* Recognize possible process and product improvements and actively implement such improvements;
* Selection of components, drawing schematics (including simulations) and re-viewing of PCB lay-outs;
* Verification and integration testing;
* Provide support and problem solving during EMC testing;
* Active participation and contributing to all design related activities. 


**Qualifications**

